# Godot and tests

## Project wiring

- One root `project.godot` for the whole lab
- Shared libraries under `engine/`; each game under `games/<name>/{sim,app,docs}/`
- New `.gd` files belong next to their owner. Scene scripts sit beside their `.tscn` under `app/`
- Do not put game rules in autoloads unless the architecture doc explicitly allows a thin lab service

## Tests (GUT, headless)

```sh
godot --path . --headless -s addons/gut/gut_cmdln.gd
```

- Options live in `.gutconfig.json` (`dirs`, empty `prefix`, `suffix` `_test.gd`, `include_subdirs`, `should_exit`)
- Suites live in `tests/engine/` and `tests/games/<name>/`
- Name test scripts `*_test.gd`; methods `test_*_should_*`
- Tests open no window (`--headless`)
- GUT is vendored under `addons/gut/` — see `docs/how-to/build-and-test.md`

When changing a module, update or add unit tests under the matching `tests/engine/` or `tests/games/<name>/` leaf. Recipes: `docs/how-to/write-headless-tests.md`.
